# =============================================================================
#  components/qmldir
# =============================================================================
#  Explicit qmldir for the components/ directory.
#
#  Why this exists:
#    In Qt 6.5+ (and especially Qt 6.11), implicit-module resolution for a
#    directory that mixes top-level .qml files with sub-directories can fail
#    with errors like:
#
#        qrc:/qt/qml/bookclub/client/qml/publisher/PublisherShell.qml:279:25:
#        AppIcon is not a type
#
#    even when AppIcon.qml is present in the imported directory. Adding an
#    explicit qmldir that lists every type defined directly in this folder
#    removes the ambiguity and makes the type registration deterministic.
#
#  Notes:
#    • This file intentionally does NOT declare a `module` name. It is a
#      "local" qmldir consumed by path-based imports (e.g.
#      `import "../components"`), which is how every consumer in this
#      project imports it.
#    • Sub-directories (buttons/, navigation/, feedback/, ...) each have
#      their own .qml files and rely on their own implicit modules; they
#      are NOT declared here.
# =============================================================================
AppIcon 1.0 AppIcon.qml
NetworkImage 1.0 NetworkImage.qml
